            "contribution_type": "deletion",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "Central air conditioning (AC) is a wonderful thing—except when it isn't practical. You may have a second building that needs AC, or a refurbished garage or attic that swelters in the summer. You can use the windows, but those are bulky, noisy, and cut out 50% of the window light. The solution? An in-wall air conditioner! They're quiet, efficient, and will keep you cool!"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "{{nointroimg}}Central air conditioning (AC) is a wonderful thing—except when it isn't practical. You may have a second building that needs AC, or a refurbished garage or attic that swelters in the summer. You can use the windows, but those are bulky, noisy, and cut out 50% of the window light. The solution? An in-wall air conditioner! They're quiet, efficient, and will keep you cool!"
                ]
            }
        },
