                    "#*Remove the center stud(s) if needed to accommodate the AC unit.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 3Bullet6.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "# Transfer the dimensions of the AC unit or sleeve to the inside of the outside wall.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 4.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Create the hole for the outside of the unit. Mark the outside opening using a template if provided by the AC manufacturer, or draw one in.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 5.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "# Build supports. Cut a stud to fit against the two studs that make the sides of the opening created for the AC unit.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 6.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Cut two (2 x 4 construction) or three (2 x 6 construction) pieces of the same length from a 2-by. Cut one or two (again, 1 for 2x4 or 2 for 2x6 construction) strips of 1/2\" plywood the same size as the 2-bys.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet1.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Place the plywood strips between the 2-bys and nail or screw together. The completed header thickness should be very close to 3-1/2 or 5-1/2 inches (for 2x4 or 2x6 construction, respectively).<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Cut two 2-bys equal to the opening height. Secure them against the existing studs in the space for the unit, by resting on the bottom horizontal support previously installed and nail or screw in place.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet3.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Rest the header on top of the vertical supports installed in the previous step.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet4.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Secure the header by nailing or screwing in place.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet5.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Add studs. Cut a 2-by to fit between the header and the top plate (the 2-by that the left- and right-most studs are secured to at the top) plus 1/8 inch at the left-most stud and nail or screw into place.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 8.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Finish the frame. Cut two 2-bys equal to the height of the opening. Making this cut a little long (1/16 inch or so) will help ensure settling will not reduce the opening and minimize any movement. Hammer these 2-bys along the left and right side of the opening. Nail or screw in place.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 9.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "# Install any [[Add an Electrical Outlet to a Wall|electrical outlets]] required while the wall is open.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 10.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Reinstall the insulation.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 11Bullet1.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Install the [[Tape and Mud Drywall|drywall]].<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 11Bullet2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Tape, mud (joint compound) and sand when dry.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 11Bullet3.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#*Paint wall and reinstall all molding.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 11Bullet4.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "# Install the AC unit. Remove unit front cover and screws that hold the unit inside its case.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 12.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "# Caulk around the unit.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 13.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "# Install molding. Add trim around the unit inside by cutting appropriate length boards at a 45-degree. Secure with finish nails. Set and fill nail heads and paint.<br><br>[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 14.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    ""
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "# [[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 1.jpg|right|300px]]Pick a location where the AC will be installed. Try not to locate above electrics and electronics because they may be damaged by condensation from the discharge air grates on very humid days.",
                    "# [[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 2.jpg|right|300px]][[Find a Wood Stud in a Wall to Hang Pictures On|Locate the wall studs]]. Use a stud finder, visually inspect baseboards for nail heads, or rap on the walls with your knuckles—you can hear the sound change from hollow to solid as you rap over a stud. (Commonly, studs are 16 inches apart in the U.S.)",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 2Bullet1.jpg|right|300px]]Lightly indicate with pencil on the wall where these studs lie.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 2Bullet2.jpg|right|300px]]Roughly indicate the layout of the AC unit on the wall, in such a way that the number of studs to be removed are minimized.",
                    "#[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 3.jpg|right|300px]]Clear the area. Remove any molding above and below the intended opening location.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 3Bullet1.jpg|right|300px]]Remove the drywall between those studs indicated from the floor to the ceiling first by scoring the wall with a razor blade (utility knife) along the inside of the studs.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 3Bullet2.jpg|right|300px]]With a hammer or gloved fist, knock out just enough drywall to locate any wires or other obstructions that could be damaged with a saw.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 3Bullet3.jpg|right|300px]]Use of a utility knife works surprisingly well on drywall, and will result in the least amount of dust and risk of damaging wires and pipes in the wall space. To use the knife, repeatedly score the wall top to bottom. You do not need to completely penetrate through the drywall—just get through 1/2 to 3/4 of the thickness. A sharp hit on the wall with a gloved fist will break the drywall along the scored line.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 3Bullet4.jpg|right|300px]]Alternately, you can saw out the drywall by cutting as close as possible to the side of the studs. Use of hand saws made for drywall will minimize dust. If using a Sawzall or similar, a helper with a vacuum following your cutting path will reduce dust considerably.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 3Bullet5.jpg|right|300px]]Remove the insulation.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 3Bullet6.jpg|right|300px]]Remove the center stud(s) if needed to accommodate the AC unit.",
                    "# [[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 4.jpg|right|300px]]Transfer the dimensions of the AC unit or sleeve to the inside of the outside wall.",
                    "#[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 5.jpg|right|300px]]Create the hole for the outside of the unit. Mark the outside opening using a template if provided by the AC manufacturer, or draw one in.",
                    "# [[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 6.jpg|right|300px]]Build supports. Cut a stud to fit against the two studs that make the sides of the opening created for the AC unit.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet1.jpg|right|300px]]Cut two (2 x 4 construction) or three (2 x 6 construction) pieces of the same length from a 2-by. Cut one or two (again, 1 for 2x4 or 2 for 2x6 construction) strips of 1/2\" plywood the same size as the 2-bys.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet2.jpg|right|300px]]Place the plywood strips between the 2-bys and nail or screw together. The completed header thickness should be very close to 3-1/2 or 5-1/2 inches (for 2x4 or 2x6 construction, respectively).",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet3.jpg|right|300px]]Cut two 2-bys equal to the opening height. Secure them against the existing studs in the space for the unit, by resting on the bottom horizontal support previously installed and nail or screw in place.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet4.jpg|right|300px]]Rest the header on top of the vertical supports installed in the previous step.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet5.jpg|right|300px]]Secure the header by nailing or screwing in place.",
                    "#[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 8.jpg|right|300px]]Add studs. Cut a 2-by to fit between the header and the top plate (the 2-by that the left- and right-most studs are secured to at the top) plus 1/8 inch at the left-most stud and nail or screw into place.",
                    "#[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 9.jpg|right|300px]]Finish the frame. Cut two 2-bys equal to the height of the opening. Making this cut a little long (1/16 inch or so) will help ensure settling will not reduce the opening and minimize any movement. Hammer these 2-bys along the left and right side of the opening. Nail or screw in place.",
                    "# [[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 10.jpg|right|300px]]Install any [[Add an Electrical Outlet to a Wall|electrical outlets]] required while the wall is open.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 11Bullet1.jpg|right|300px]]Reinstall the insulation.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 11Bullet2.jpg|right|300px]]Install the [[Tape and Mud Drywall|drywall]].",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 11Bullet3.jpg|right|300px]]Tape, mud (joint compound) and sand when dry.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 11Bullet4.jpg|right|300px]]Paint wall and reinstall all molding.",
                    "# [[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 12.jpg|right|300px]]Install the AC unit. Remove unit front cover and screws that hold the unit inside its case.",
                    "# [[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 13.jpg|right|300px]]Caulk around the unit.",
                    "# [[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 14.jpg|right|300px]]Install molding. Add trim around the unit inside by cutting appropriate length boards at a 45-degree. Secure with finish nails. Set and fill nail heads and paint."
                ]
            }
