                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet2.jpg|right|300px]]Place the plywood strips between the 2-bys and nail or screw together. The completed header thickness should be very close to 3-1/2 or 5-1/2 inches (for 2x4 or 2x6 construction, respectively).",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet3.jpg|right|300px]]Cut two 2-bys equal to the opening height. Secure them against the existing studs in the space for the unit, by resting on the bottom horizontal support previously installed and nail or screw in place.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet4.jpg|right|300px]]Rest the header on top of the vertical supports installed in the previous step.",
                    "#*[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 7Bullet5.jpg|right|300px]]Secure the header by nailing or screwing in place.",
                    "#[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 8.jpg|right|300px]]Add studs. Cut a 2-by to fit between the header and the top plate (the 2-by that the left- and right-most studs are secured to at the top) plus 1/8 inch at the left-most stud and nail or screw into place.",
                    "#[[Image:Install an Inwall Air Conditioner Step 9.jpg|right|300px]]Finish the frame. Cut two 2-bys equal to the height of the opening. Making this cut a little long (1/16 inch or so) will help ensure settling will not reduce the opening and minimize any movement. Hammer these 2-bys along the left and right side of the opening. Nail or screw in place.",
